koelab — Terms of Use

Copyright (c) 2026 Arimino-1213. All rights reserved.

Effective: September 27, 2026

(The Japanese version above is the authoritative text. This English version is a reference translation; in case of any discrepancy, the Japanese version prevails.)

1. Scope and ownership
   1.1 These terms govern the use of the source code, documents, images and all other materials in the GitHub repository Arimino-1213/koelab (the "Software") and of the application provided at https://arimino-1213.github.io/koelab/ (the "App").
   1.2 All copyright and other rights in the Software belong to the author (GitHub account Arimino-1213, the "Author"). Except as set out in Section 2, no rights in the Software are granted.

2. Permitted uses
   You may, without permission from the Author:
   (1) view the Software on GitHub;
   (2) fork the Software within GitHub's functionality, as provided in the GitHub Terms of Service (Section D.5); forking grants no rights beyond those in these terms, and publishing the App from a forked repository (including via GitHub Pages) constitutes publishing under Section 3(3);
   (3) use the App as an individual by accessing the public URL (including the Software being loaded into your browser as part of that use); and
   (4) make any use permitted by law without the right holder's consent, such as reproduction for private use under Article 30 of the Japanese Copyright Act.

3. Prohibited acts
   Without the Author's prior permission (in writing or by electronic means such as email), you must not:
   (1) reproduce all or part of the Software (except as permitted in Section 2);
   (2) modify or adapt the Software, or incorporate or reuse it in other software or services;
   (3) redistribute, sell, lend, or publish the Software (including modified versions) on any other website or server;
   (4) use the Software (including modified versions) to provide a commercial service or for any other commercial purpose;
   (5) remove or alter any copyright notice or these terms; or
   (6) use the App in violation of laws, public order and morals, or the terms of Google or any other third party, or in a way that infringes the rights or interests of others.

4. Third-party components
   4.1 At runtime, the App loads the following third-party components from their distributors. They are not part of the Software and remain subject to their own licenses:
       - mp4-muxer (MIT License)
       - lamejs (GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0)
       - Noto Sans JP / Noto Sans SC (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
   4.2 These terms do not restrict any rights granted to you by the licenses of those components (including modifying or replacing them and any analysis needed to do so).

5. External services and voice replication
   5.1 The App's AI features (transcription, text-to-speech, voice replication, etc.) are used between you and Google with a Google Gemini API key that you obtain yourself. You must comply with the Gemini API Additional Terms of Service (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms), the Generative AI Prohibited Use Policy (https://policies.google.com/terms/generative-ai/use-policy) and any other Google terms. Fees, usage limits and the handling of data you send are governed by Google.
   5.2 Voice replication requires the consent of the person whose voice it is. You must not register another person's voice without their consent, impersonate a person with a registered voice, publish statements the person did not make as if they were the person's own, or otherwise harm the rights or interests of that person or any third party.
   5.3 The Author claims no rights in the audio, video or other output you create with the App. You use such output at your own responsibility.

6. No warranty
   The Software and the App are provided "as is". The Author makes no warranty of any kind, including accuracy, completeness, fitness for a particular purpose, or continued availability. The Author may change the App or stop providing it at any time without notice.

7. Limitation of liability
   7.1 The Author is not liable for any damage arising in connection with the Software or the App, except in the case of the Author's willful misconduct or gross negligence.
   7.2 Section 7.1 does not apply if the relationship between you and the Author constitutes a consumer contract as defined in Article 2(3) of the Japanese Consumer Contract Act. In that case, the Author's liability for damage caused by the Author's ordinary negligence (negligence other than willful misconduct or gross negligence), whether in contract or in tort, is limited to direct and ordinary damage actually incurred by you.

8. Requests for permission
   To request permission for any act listed in Section 3, contact the Author via the repository's Issues or the contact information on the Author's GitHub profile.

9. Governing law
   These terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of Japan.
